From 759c7ffcd40be7166b1486dad70ef06e4aaa1002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: apple: j71t: reserve the sepOS root
 shared-memory page

pongoOS booted sepOS on 2026-10-26 with op 6 and handed it a one-page
root shared-memory buffer on endpoint 0xfe at PA 0x87adb0000. XNU keeps
its equivalent buffer for the lifetime of the system, so sepOS may read
or write that page at any time. It lies inside the System RAM range
m1n1 gives Linux (0x800000000-0x87b7fffff) and nothing reserved it; it
only escaped reuse because the crashkernel=256M reservation happened to
land on 0x86b800000-0x87b7fffff.

Mark it no-map. 16 KiB covers the 4 KiB buffer with this kernel's page
size. No label, so the node gets no phandle and the warm-kexec FDT merge
has nothing to renumber.

The address is a runtime value of that pongoOS session: if sepOS is
booted again, read the "root shmem ... data=" line of the pongoOS log and
update this node. The durable fix is for pongoOS/m1n1 to publish it.

The SEPFW staging region (0x804f48000, 0x344000 bytes) is deliberately not
reserved: XNU releases it (ml_static_mfree, and removes SEPFW from
/chosen/memory-map) as soon as sepOS reports alive, so SEPROM does not
need it after the op 6 load.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
index 274e41c1da..5c1d45752e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003-j71t.dts
@@ -27,6 +27,18 @@ nvme_hmb: nvme-hmb@0 {
 			reg = <0 0 0 0>; /* To be filled by loader */
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * sepOS root shared-memory page, handed over by pongoOS with
+		 * op 6 on endpoint 0xfe (2026-10-26 boot: data=87adb0). sepOS
+		 * may use it for the rest of its life. The address belongs to
+		 * that pongoOS session: after a new sepOS boot, take it from
+		 * the "root shmem ... data=" line of the pongoOS log.
+		 */
+		sep-shmem@87adb0000 {
+			reg = <0x8 0x7adb0000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
